Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||03-20-2001||10:23 AM||||2 days ago my mom called me and said there's something wrong with the car, it's making a grinding noise from the left front wheel when it moved back and forth. Anyway, this morning my dad called and asked me if I hit any bumps or potholes when I was home for spring break 2 weeks ago, cause BOTH front springs are broken as well as the drivers side front strut....<BR>The car was fine when I was driving it, and it was fine for a week and a half when my mom was driving it after I came back to school. Apparently it just broke while sitting in the driveway overnight.<P>I don't recall hitting any big bumps recently, and neither does my mom. I've damaged the suspension in the past, when I got the car stuck in a snowbank during the first winter I had my license, but that was in 1999.. and I backed into a ditch one time too, but that didn't involve the front suspension.. and the car drove fine after that..<P><B>Is it possible that 2 springs ad a strut can just snap on their own, while sitting in a driveway?</B> I think if I'd hit anything to break them, then they would have broken right then.. but no one noticed any problems until 2 days ago, and my mom had been driving the car regularly before that, after I went back to school. My dad doesn't believe me that I didn't hit anything on spring break, and he's pretty mad..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>p.s. it's a 1995 Ford Taurus SE<P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||5
